{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1763,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The most famous computer bug in history was an actual bug, trapped inside a giant machine.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 120
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Harvard, September ninth, nineteen forty-seven. The Mark II computer was being tested. It was a room full of relays, tiny switches that a magnet clicks shut.",
   "from": 124,
   "to": 343
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But that afternoon, right in the middle of a test, the operators traced an error.",
   "from": 346,
   "to": 455
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "They searched the whole machine, panel by panel, relay by relay.",
   "from": 458,
   "to": 552
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "At fifteen forty-five, in Panel F, Relay number seventy, they found it: a moth, trapped between the contact points.",
   "from": 556,
   "to": 735
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "They pulled it out, taped it into the logbook, and wrote one line.",
   "from": 739,
   "to": 832
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "operator",
   "text": "First actual case of bug being found.",
   "from": 836,
   "to": 904
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But why the word actual?",
   "from": 908,
   "to": 946
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, a relay works only when its two contacts touch. The magnet pulls them together, and the current flows on. With a moth's body in the way, they could not close.",
   "from": 959,
   "to": 1206
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And the word bug was already old. Thomas Edison wrote about bugs back in eighteen seventy-eight.",
   "from": 1209,
   "to": 1337
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The joke stuck, and Grace Hopper, who worked on the machine, told the story again and again.",
   "from": 1341,
   "to": 1495
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So today the page, moth and all, is kept at the Smithsonian's National Museum of American History.",
   "from": 1498,
   "to": 1639
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And the first actual bug is still taped right there on that page.",
   "from": 1643,
   "to": 1739
  }
 ],
